---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';

const aboutSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "AboutPage",
      "@id": "https://www.wanderwithakhi.com/about/#webpage",
      "url": "https://www.wanderwithakhi.com/about/",
      "name": "About Akhilesh Gowda | The Seeker-Engineer behind Wander with Akhi",
      "description": "The story of Akhilesh Gowda: from corporate software engineer to traditional Indian ashrams, slow travel, and somatic healing.",
      "breadcrumb": {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "itemListElement": [
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 1,
            "name": "Home",
            "item": "https://www.wanderwithakhi.com/"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": "About",
            "item": "https://www.wanderwithakhi.com/about/"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Person",
      "@id": "https://www.wanderwithakhi.com/#author",
      "name": "Akhilesh Gowda",
      "alternateName": "Akhi",
      "url": "https://www.wanderwithakhi.com/",
      "image": "https://www.wanderwithakhi.com/images/about_akhi.jpg",
      "jobTitle": "Slow Travel Writer, Yogic Seeker & Founder",
      "description": "Former corporate software engineer turned traditional spiritual seeker and slow travel author, writing at the intersection of nervous system restoration, authentic yoga retreats, and Vedic philosophy in India.",
      "sameAs": [
        "https://www.instagram.com/wanderwithakhi",
        "https://ayush.gov.in/",
        "https://karnatakatourism.org/"
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="About Akhilesh Gowda | The Seeker-Engineer | Wander with Akhi"
  description="Discover the story behind Wander with Akhi: how a rural Indian engineer left corporate desk fatigue to discover 7 months of silent ashram sadhana in Mysore, slow travel, and somatic nervous system recovery."
  image="/images/about_akhi.jpg"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(aboutSchema)} />
  <Header />

  <main class="about-page">
    {/* Hero Manifesto Section */}
    <section class="about-hero">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <span class="about-badge">Author & Seeker's Manifesto</span>
        <h1 class="about-title">Wandering Outside & Inside</h1>
        <p class="about-lead">
          "Exploring the world without checking in with yourself is just moving. Sitting still without understanding the world around you is just isolation. I write at the intersection of both."
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* Narrative Story Section */}
    <section class="about-story-section">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <div class="author-portrait-card">
          <img 
            src="/images/about_akhi.jpg" 
            alt="Akhilesh Gowda meditating in contemplative stillness at the sacred Adiyogi sanctum in South India" 
            class="author-img"
            loading="eager"
          />
          <div class="author-caption">
            <strong>Akhilesh Gowda (Akhi)</strong>
            <span>Yogic Seeker, Slow Travel Author & Co-Founder</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <article class="story-content">
          <h2>The Corporate Screen & The Quiet Emptiness</h2>
          <p>
            Like many raised in traditional Indian villages, my trajectory was planned long before I understood my own nervous system. I pursued an engineering degree, graduated, and landed what was considered the ideal prize: a corporate tech job in coastal Goa.
          </p>
          <p>
            For a few years, I lived the accepted script—long hours staring into glowing monitors, eating on the run, living for Friday night parties, and dreaming of two-week holiday sprints. But underneath the corporate stability lay an insidious chronic exhaustion. My physical posture deteriorated, digestive fires weakened, and an persistent inner emptiness began to ask: <em>Is this entire existence meant to be spent waiting for the weekend?</em>
          </p>
          <p>
            When the global pandemic struck and the world ground to a sudden halt, the forced isolation shattered whatever illusions I had left. I realized that climbing a corporate ladder in a high-cortisol environment was quietly destroying my health. I needed a complete reset.
          </p>

          <hr class="story-divider" />

          <h2>Seven Months in a Mysore Ashram: The Rebirth of Sadhana</h2>
          <p>
            In search of physical and mental restoration, I packed a single duffel bag and left for <strong>Mysore</strong>—the global heritage capital of Ashtanga yoga. I had initially planned to volunteer my digital design skills at a traditional ashram for a single month to clear my head.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>I stayed for seven months.</strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            Living under ashram discipline completely dismantled my old operating system:
          </p>
          <ul class="story-bullet-list">
            <li><strong>Circadian Re-alignment:</strong> Waking with the pre-dawn Brahma Muhurta (5:00 AM) to the sound of temple bells and chanting, synchronizing natural melatonin and cortisol curves.</li>
            <li><strong>Sattvic Nutrition:</strong> Transitioning to clean, locally sourced, vegetarian and Ayurvedic meals that healed chronic digestive inflammation.</li>
            <li><strong>Rigorous Sadhana:</strong> Daily immersion in classical Hatha and Ashtanga asanas, functional anatomy, and direct study of the Patanjali Yoga Sutras and Vedanta philosophy.</li>
            <li><strong>Noble Silence (Mouna):</strong> Experiencing the profound cognitive restoration that happens when the mouth stops talking and the mind stops performing.</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="story-divider" />

          <h2>Why Wander with Akhi Exists: The Three Pillars</h2>
          <p>
            When I eventually stepped back out into the world, I looked at travel through transformed eyes. I saw thousands of international travelers arriving in India seeking spiritual rejuvenation, only to be overwhelmed by commercial party noise, predatory tourist scams, or superficial wellness trends.
          </p>
          <p>
            I created <strong>Wander with Akhi</strong> to be the definitive, grounded bridge between ancient Indian wisdom and the modern seeker’s reality:
          </p>

          <div class="pillars-grid">
            <div class="pillar-box">
              <span class="pillar-num">01</span>
              <h3>The Outer Journey</h3>
              <p>Unbiased, zero-sponsored field guides to authentic yoga retreats, silent ashrams, and quietcation coordinates in Goa, Mysore, Kerala, and the Himalayas.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="pillar-box">
              <span class="pillar-num">02</span>
              <h3>The Somatic Science</h3>
              <p>Translating ancient yogic practices into modern neuroscience—vagal nerve regulation, heart rate variability (HRV), fascial biomechanics, and jetlag recovery.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="pillar-box">
              <span class="pillar-num">03</span>
              <h3>The Inner Journey</h3>
              <p>Philosophical deep dives into Kashmir Shaivism, Vedanta, Swara breath science, and daily Dinacharya rituals you can practice anywhere in the world.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <hr class="story-divider" />

          <h2>My Personal Promise to You</h2>
          <p>
            Everything on this website is written from direct lived sadhana. You will not find sponsored fluff, paid placement rankings, or AI-generated tourist clichés here. Whether you are an exhausted corporate professional planning your first 200-hour teacher training in Goa, an introvert seeking a silent Vipassana sanctuary, or a mindful nomad searching for slower paths—I am here to guide you home to your breath.
          </p>

          <div class="author-signoff">
            <p class="signoff-quote">"Walk slow. Breathe deep. Wander both outside and inside."</p>
            <span class="signoff-name">— Akhilesh Gowda (Akhi)</span>
          </div>

          <div class="about-action-bar">
            <a href="/guide" class="btn-primary">Explore Digital Workbooks &rarr;</a>
            <a href="/#outside" class="btn-secondary">Read Destination Guides &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    padding-bottom: 6rem;
  }

  .narrow {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-hero {
    padding: 5rem 0 3rem;
    text-align: center;
    border-bottom: var(--border-thin);
  }

  .about-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .about-title {
    font-family: var(--font-syne, 'Syne', sans-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.8rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-lead {
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 650px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .about-story-section {
    padding-top: 3.5rem;
  }

  .author-portrait-card {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .author-img {
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 480px;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center top;
    border-radius: 12px;
    border: var(--border-thin);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
  }

  .author-caption {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }

  .author-caption strong {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .author-caption span {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .story-content h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-syne, 'Syne', sans-serif);
    font-size: 1.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .story-content p {
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .story-divider {
    border: 0;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--border-thin-color, #e5e5e5);
    margin: 3rem 0;
  }

  .story-bullet-list {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .pillars-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .pillars-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .pillar-box {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--color-surface, #fafafa);
    border: var(--border-thin);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .pillar-num {
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .pillar-box h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .pillar-box p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .author-signoff {
    margin: 3.5rem 0 2.5rem;
    padding: 2rem;
    background: var(--color-surface, #f9f9f9);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
  }

  .signoff-quote {
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .signoff-name {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    display: block;
  }

  .about-action-bar {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .btn-primary, .btn-secondary {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.6rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    border-radius: 6px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--color-text);
    color: var(--color-bg, #ffffff);
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    opacity: 0.9;
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }

  .btn-secondary {
    border: var(--border-thin);
    color: var(--color-text);
    background: transparent;
  }

  .btn-secondary:hover {
    background: var(--color-surface, #f5f5f5);
  }
</style>
